1. Definitions

1.1 'Licence' means this CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Strongly 
Reciprocal.

1.2 'Source' means information in any form (including, but not limited to, 
schematics, layout designs, computer-aided design files, software, 
firmware, documentation and text) describing the Product and/or the Object 
Code, and reasonably necessary for maintaining, manufacturing, and/or 
using the Product.

1.3 'Product' means any physical object or device manufactured or 
assembled based on the Source.

1.4 'Object Code' means the digital representation of the Source 
resulting from its compilation, translation or execution by a computer or 
similar machine.

1.5 'Licensee' (or 'you') means any natural or legal person exercising 
rights under this Licence.

1.6 'Licensor' means any natural or legal person who grants rights under 
this Licence.

1.7 'Contributor' means any natural or legal person who Modifies the 
Source or the Object Code, and makes the resulting work available under 
this Licence.

1.8 'Modify' (or 'Modification') means to alter the Source or the Object 
Code, or to perform any work that is based on the Source or the Object 
Code or that incorporates the Source or the Object Code.

1.9 'Convey' (or 'Conveyance') means to make the Source, the Object Code 
or the Product available to any third party, whether by sale, lease, loan, 
gift, or any other form of transfer or distribution.


