3. Conditions and Reciprocity

The grants under Section 2 are subject to the following conditions:

3.1 Notices

You must preserve and maintain all copyright, patent, trademark and 
licence notices, and any disclaimers, present in the Source you receive.

3.2 Modifications

a) If you Modify the Source or the Object Code, you must include a notice 
in the Modified Source or Object Code stating that you have modified it, 
and providing the date and a brief description of the Modification.

b) If you Convey Modified Source, you must do so under the terms of this 
Licence or, if the Licensor has specified that a later version of the 
CERN Open Hardware Licence applies, under the terms of this Licence or 
that later version.

c) If you Convey Modified Object Code or a Product based on Modified 
Source, you must make the Source for such Modified Object Code or Product 
available to the recipient, under the terms of this Licence, in one of the 
following ways:

i) by including it with the Conveyance; or
ii) by providing a written offer, valid for at least three years, to state 
where the Source can be obtained; or
iii) if you provide the Object Code or Product via a network or specific 
website, by providing a link or uniform resource identifier to the Source 
on the same network or website, or a similarly accessible location.

3.3 Strong Reciprocity

a) The complete Source for any Product or Object Code that you Convey 
under Section 3.2(c) must be licensed under this Licence, including any 
components, parts or subsystems that you have added or Modified.

b) The requirement in Section 3.3(a) applies to any part of the Source that 
is required to form a fully operational and compatible Product or Object 
Code, even if such parts could be considered independent works in their 
own right.


